[center][i]Built to work the way AAF intends, with thanks to [b]Dagobaking[/b], author of AAF, for his technical guidance. Our notes on AAF are [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport/issues/1]reviewed by him[/url], and his word is final.[/i][/center]

[center][size=4][b][url=https://pixeldrain.com/u/7ZnoDbUt]▶ Watch the demo[/url][/b][/size] (1:16, the Third Rail: voiced lines, subtitles, bystanders)[/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[center][b]The Commonwealth family: made to work together[/b]
[b]Rapport[/b] (this page): runs the scenes · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109225]Chemistry[/url]: NPCs find each other · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109433]Overture[/url]: you talk someone into it · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy[/url]: working genitals, arousal and contact · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109434]Anatomy Engine[/url]: the physics behind them · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109439]Silhouette[/url]: everyone gets a body of their own · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/fallout4/collections/dmt85e]Ivy's Panties[/url]: all of it, installed for you[/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]What it is[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Rapport is a framework, not a story.[/b] AAF plays animations; Rapport runs the scene around them. Addons decide [i]when[/i]: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109225]Chemistry[/url] lets NPCs find each other, and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109433]Overture[/url] lets you walk up to someone and try your luck. Rapport alone starts nothing.

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/family.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]New in 0.2.5[/color][/b][/size]

[center][size=4][b]Moans timed to each stroke Anatomy's physics measures, in each NPC's own voice and temperament.[/b][/size][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/moans.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Scene moans.[/b] 419 takes, 2 voices × 4 temperaments; painful pleasure for the receiver, a climax that lands. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6668]Scenes and pairing →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/wardrobe.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Nobody left naked.[/b] AAF re-dresses only on a clean ending; Rapport's own snapshot, kept in the save, puts back what is missing. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/identity.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Change who they are.[/b] Face anyone, press a hotkey: orientation or persona, this save only. Every family mod follows. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6669]Relationships and people →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/glances.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Faces that fit the act, and eye contact.[/b] Packs give faces to 0.4% of actions; Rapport classifies 99.2%. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/voices-map.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]Every character speaks.[/b] 6,656 recordings; 629 voice types fingerprinted, so unique characters borrow the closest voice. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@667b7437e1bb0aeb54c16553297ec406c0af5d21/docs/img/narrator.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][b]The Narrator.[/b] Who, why and the score part by part; all four moments on by default. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6670]The Narrator →[/url][/center]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Everything else, one line each[/color][/b][/size]

[b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6668]Scenes and pairing →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]The whole tree is read: the scene asked for, to a real ending.
[*]A 600 s stop: no scene runs forever.
[*]Same-sex pairs prefer their own animations, never an empty scene (new).
[*]Never anyone unconscious, restrained or frozen; nothing before Vault 111.
[/list]
[b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces, voices and bodies →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]Faces nothing can close: Anatomy's hook acts after the engine's merge.
[*]Real dialogue with lip sync; every take checked against its subtitle.
[*]Aftermath in game hours, on the receiver: 4 by default, 1-48 on the MCM.
[*]No holstered pistol during sex, with Visible Favorites (new).
[/list]
[b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6669]Relationships and people →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]A bond from −1 to +1 between everyone who touched, seeded from the game's own ranks.
[*]Four kinds of people, spread evenly and stable forever.
[*]Bystanders notice: one roll per scene, about 1 in 3 speak.
[/list]
[b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6672]Under the hood, and for mod authors →[/url][/b]
[list]
[*]It cannot crash your game through the script engine: Papyrus asks, C++ answers.
[*]At most one AAF call per poll: other mods' scripts never stall.
[*]Refusals told from starts: no phantom scenes, no frozen NPCs.
[*]0.004-0.028 ms a pass for 49-78 actors: zero script lag.
[*]Addon door, ApiVersion 205, and our notes on AAF for any author.
[/list]

[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport@79c928255c6aee7b2b2b3b6a6f69c18a31ae978f/docs/img/divider.png[/img][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Open source, and built in public[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Source:[/b] [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport]github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport[/url], GPL-3.0, all of it. Every commit is built on a clean [url=https://github.com/ReidenXerx/fo4-rapport/actions]GitHub Actions[/url] runner, which publishes the DLL's SHA256 in a log nobody can edit afterwards.
[*][b]Honest about the build:[/b] the DLL in the download is built on our machine, with a different compiler toolset than the public build, so their hashes differ. The public build proves the source compiles; it cannot prove your download byte for byte.
[*][b]Scanned:[/b] the VirusTotal badge above is generated from the scan result and names the build it is about.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Before you play[/color][/b][/size]

[quote]
[b]Install with Vortex or MO2; manual installs are not supported.[/b] The installer refuses to run without AAF and LooksMenu. [b]Optional:[/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/109435]Anatomy 1.2.0[/url] for the moans and sex sounds, MCM, Commonwealth Moisturizer for the aftermath, Visible Favorites for the holster hiding. Upgrading from 0.2.4 mid-save is safe.

[b]Don't fast travel in the ~10 seconds while two NPCs walk to each other to start a scene[/b] (fixed in AAF 1.7.8; the public AAF is still 1.7.4.1). Once the scene has started, fast travel is safe. The crash is inside AAF's interface while the area unloads; a mod gets no warning that a fast travel is coming, and no distance setting removes the window.

[b]Nothing starts until you leave Vault 111.[/b] No scene and no approach during the game's opening, from character creation to the vault door; alternate starts and MS Skip Prewar Sanctuary work as expected. Using an unusual alternate start that never finishes the opening? MCM, first page, [i]Start now[/i].

[b]Old-gen or Anniversary Edition.[/b] Fallout 4 1.10.163 with F4SE 0.6.23, or the Anniversary Edition 1.11.x with F4SE 0.7.9. Both need [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/mods/108394]Runtime Database[/url]: without it the game stops at launch. Tested in game on AE 1.11.240; on 1.10.163 since 0.2.3 it awaits your reports; next-gen 1.10.984 is untested. Every class Rapport reads is checked before use, and on a mismatch Rapport turns itself off for that session and Rapport.log names it. [b]Downgraded from next-gen?[/b] Every F4SE plugin needs its old-gen build too: AAF first (Rapport needs it), then Buffout 4, Address Library, LooksMenu, Dialogue Menu Fix and the rest. A crash at launch after a downgrade is one of those or the downgrade itself, never Rapport. f4se.log lists the plugins as they load.

[b]Uninstalling?[/b] Set [font=Courier New]PanicClear=1[/font] in [font=Courier New]Data/F4SE/Plugins/Rapport.ini[/font] and load your save once first. It removes everything Rapport applied, faces and aftermath included. Nothing Rapport applies is something only Rapport can remove.
[/quote]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]Incompatibilities[/color][/b][/size]

Known conflicts, from real reports and the code. Found another one? Tell us in the Bugs tab.
[list]
[*][b]CumOverlays[/b]: its overlays would stack with Rapport's aftermath. Rapport turns them off during its own scenes, and Commonwealth Moisturizer is the only aftermath backend. Keep CumOverlays if you want it for other mods, but expect nothing from it in Rapport scenes.[/*]
[*][b]Original OCBPC (not the Anatomy Engine)[/b]: nothing breaks, but eye contact and the living faces need the Anatomy Engine's cbp.dll.[/*]
[*]Nothing else known.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#ffb62e]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Does it replace other mods?[/b]
[spoiler]AAF Sex 'Em Up and AAF Autonomy Enhanced do the same job, so if either is installed Rapport stops their quests, never deleting anything, and logs why. Commonwealth Moisturizer's own scene listener is stopped the same way while Rapport drives the aftermath. Everything else AAF plays keeps working, and Rapport adds its faces and aftermath to those scenes too.[/spoiler]

[b]Where do I report what I see?[/b]
[spoiler]The Bugs tab, with Rapport.log. Every report gets read.[/spoiler]

[b]Where is the full list of features and settings?[/b]
[spoiler]In the five articles on the Articles tab: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6668]Scenes and pairing[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6671]Faces voices and bodies[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6669]Relationships and people[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6670]The Narrator[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fallout4/articles/6672]Under the hood and for mod authors[/url]. Every MCM and Rapport.ini setting is in the sticky posts.[/spoiler]

[b]Can I stop scenes from starting?[/b]
[spoiler]Rapport starts nothing by itself: NPC scenes come from Chemistry and approaches from Overture, so turn those off (or uninstall them). Rapport keeps scoring and reporting to Rapport.log.[/spoiler]

